  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0301",
      "reading_order": 368,
      "section": "External battery connection",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 722.8676629101562,
        "r": 541.4523999999998,
        "b": 682.196101363195
      },
      "content": "Connect the battery cable between the (+B\\-B) battery terminal and battery switch of UPS. The connection of cable between battery terminal and battery switch should start from switch end. Pay attention to the polarity of battery cable."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0302",
      "reading_order": 369,
      "section": "External battery connection",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 676.0676629101563,
        "r": 541.2662399999996,
        "b": 650.996101363195
      },
      "content": "Inspect  wiring  and  fasten  bolt  again  for  wire  locking.  Recover  all  protective  covers  after confirmation."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0303",
      "reading_order": 370,
      "section": "3.8.2 Wiring of Parallel UPS System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 74.664,
        "t": 633.1959829101563,
        "r": 286.24600000000004,
        "b": 622.4328447886094
      },
      "content": "3.8.2 Wiring of Parallel UPS System",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0304",
      "reading_order": 371,
      "section": "3.8.2 Wiring of Parallel UPS System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 72.384,
        "t": 603.2276629101563,
        "r": 217.06568,
        "b": 593.756101363195
      },
      "content": "Wiring of parallel signal cable"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0305",
      "reading_order": 372,
      "section": "3.8.2 Wiring of Parallel UPS System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 587.6276629101563,
        "r": 541.5667199999998,
        "b": 515.726101363195
      },
      "content": "Each UPS has 4 parallel wiring ports (two are DB25 and another two are DB9). Closed loop should be formed in the wiring of DB25 in parallel system, so should DB9. Two parallel wires in the same circuit should be closed and parallel as near as possible and kept away from power cable to the greatest extent so as to reduce outside interference to parallel wires. Schematic diagram of wiring is as shown in Figure 3-27."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0058",
      "reading_order": 373,
      "section": "3.8.2 Wiring of Parallel UPS System",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 128.5850037679624,
        "t": 500.11857530560275,
        "r": 482.42854380583503,
        "b": 408.4868727160967
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0058.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0305",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0306",
